  {
   "name": "Oat Field",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pad",
   "tags": [
    "supersaw",
    "unison",
    "drift",
    "wide",
    "evolving"
   ],
   "description": "Seven-voice HQ supersaw with a supersaw-style detune curve, random unison phases and extra stereo width, slowly drifting in pitch and cutoff like an old polysynth. Each chord opens slowly; the detune breathes in and out over eleven seconds while a second slow LFO moves the cutoff, and every note gets its own detune and brightness. Mod wheel: resonance; aftertouch: brighter and wider. Macros: brightness, width, drift.",
