  {
   "name": "Fuzz Lead",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "lead",
   "tags": [
    "mono",
    "fuzz",
    "convolution",
    "cabinet"
   ],
   "description": "Two detuned saws through an asymmetric clipper (4x oversampled) after the filter, so the clipper sees every harmonic and the two saws grind against each other, then a 1×12 guitar cabinet (convolved) takes the fizz off. Held notes swell into more fuzz like an amp feeding back, the pick attack and the beat between the saws change from note to note, and a random LFO wobbles the tone. It starts as a crunch: the mod wheel turns it into full fuzz; aftertouch sweeps a resonant wah in front of the clipper. Macros: fuzz, cutoff, cabinet.",
   "params": {
    "O1_Waveform": 6,
