  {
   "name": "Chew Bass",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "per-voice drive",
    "diode ladder",
    "mono",
    "PWM"
   ],
   "description": "A resonant diode ladder chewing in front of an asymmetric drive on the voice: the filter envelope and an eighth-note LFO keep the resonant peak moving, the square under the saw slowly changes width, and the drive after it turns the peak into a snarl. Velocity adds drive and envelope, and low notes are driven harder than high ones, so the line grows teeth as it goes down. Mod wheel: the LFO goes to sixteenths; aftertouch: resonance. Macros: chew, drive, cutoff.",
