  {
   "name": "Talk Bass",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "bass",
   "tags": [
    "formant",
    "vowel",
    "mono",
    "compressor"
   ],
   "description": "A bass that talks: a saw and a square an octave down through a formant filter. Each note's mod envelope sweeps the vowel from its own starting point and an eighth-note LFO makes held notes yap, then a soft drive, a compressor and a bass-mono utility keep it solid. Mod wheel: the LFO goes to sixteenths; aftertouch: opens the vowel. Macros: talk, vowel, drive.",
