  {
   "name": "Squash Pluck",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "pluck",
   "tags": [
    "supersaw",
    "compressor",
    "OTT",
    "delay"
   ],
   "description": "A bright supersaw pluck squashed OTT-style by the three-band compressor: downward compression tames the attack and upward compression lifts the tail and the top, so each pluck stays dense as it dies. Each pluck lands at its own place and brightness, and a slow LFO evolves the detune and cutoff across a sequence. A short tempo delay behind it. Mod wheel: resonance; velocity: a longer sweep. Macros: squash, brightness, delay.",
