  {
   "name": "Glass Spiral",
   "author": "Porridge",
   "category": "texture",
   "tags": [
    "frequency shifter",
    "bode",
    "feedback",
    "ambient"
   ],
   "description": "Glassy tones fed into the Bode frequency shifter's feedback delay: every echo comes back shifted a little higher than the last, so each note spirals up into a shimmering cloud while the dry note stays where it is. Each note's sparkle (a glassy partial) is struck and fades, its ratio cast a little differently, and a slow LFO drifts the spiral's speed. Notes land at random places in the stereo field. Mod wheel: a longer spiral; aftertouch: more of it. Macros: shift, spiral, mix.",
