   "tags": [
    "reverse reverb",
    "swell",
    "convolution",
    "tremolo"
   ],
   "description": "Plays like a sound running backwards: each note swells in on a curve that rushes at the end and stops short when let go, its filter and resonance opening with it and a tremolo speeding up into it, through a reversed hall impulse (convolution), so the reverb rises towards each note instead of trailing away from it. Mod wheel: a longer, wetter reverse; aftertouch: brighter. Macros: swell, reverse.",
